==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|urj-pro|fi}} {{term/t|urj-pro|*śüδämi}}; cognate with Estonian {{term|lang=et|süda}} and Hungarian {{term|lang=hu|szív}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|lang=fi|[ˈsydæn]}}
* ''Note:'' In colloquial speech, usually pronounced with a long ''m'' in inflections and derivations (e.g., sydämen [ˈsydæmːen]).

===Noun===
{{fi-noun}}

# [[heart]]
# [[core]]
#: {{term|lang=fi|reaktorisydän|reaktori'''sydän'''|nuclear reactor core, reactor core}}
# [[wick]] (of a candle)

